WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.886
Still post-processing USPEX the old way?

2
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:09.402
So many files — Origin, Excel, VESTA, round and round.

3
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.522
There's a better way.

4
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.698
Drop your USPEX output straight into the browser.

5
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.402
No install. No upload. Everything runs right here.

6
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.714
The whole run, at a glance.

7
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.586
Every structure, every property, in one table.

8
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.994
Each keeps its lineage: parents, offspring, variations.

9
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.962
Open any structure in 3D with one click — and spin it.

10
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:51.554
Convex hulls, from binary to quaternary, in 2D or 3D.

11
00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:54.786
Click any point to inspect the structure behind it.

12
00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:01.154
Merge runs at the same pressure — fixed or variable composition.

13
00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.954
Test a candidate: will it change the hull?

14
00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:11.266
Pareto front and hypervolume, tracked generation by generation.

15
00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.938
Watch the population evolve, one generation at a time.

16
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.626
Pick the structures you want, and export them any way you need.

17
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.018
Runs locally in your browser. Your data never leaves your machine.

18
00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:31.866
USPEX Analyzer. Give post-processing back to science.
